<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kennebec River</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kennebec River flows about 270 km from Moosehead Lake to the Atlantic in Maine, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>. The short-lived Popham Colony was planted at its mouth in 1607, and Plymouth Colony ran a fur-trading post on it at Cushnoc, now Augusta. For long it marked a frontier between English settlement, Wabanaki lands and French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acadia">Acadia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kennebec-river.jpg" alt="Kennebec River" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomsonmg2000 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:KennebecRiverinSomersetCounty.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
